    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cv-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Gateway segment of budget #6, sampled 1 in 32, first 31 frames not observed: from a subscription's turn in the hub loop to the writer handing the frame to the socket. The 20 ms line is the whole backend envelope of budget #6, and this stage is one share of it (06 section 5.1). A congested client's drain wait, a slow consumer's backlog and replay frames are inside it. WsFanoutP95OverBudget judges it only with 40 sampled frames in 5 minutes, so an empty line is a quiet gateway, not a healthy one.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "dashed"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#0072B2",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#E69F00",
                "value": 0.02
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 26
      },
      "id": 10,
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cv-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(cv_ws_fanout_seconds_bucket{env=\"$env\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "WS fan-out latency p95 (budget 20 ms)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cv-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Gateway-wide sum over the dashboard range before each point (1 h by default, which the lines are for: target under 1, hard fail above 5 an hour), rounded to whole events as WsUpstreamDesyncHigh rounds. Each affected subscription counts once, so one upstream desync adds one per subscribed topic across all connections; 23-ws-protocol.md 16.3 is per topic, so group the `ws resync` log lines by `ch`. upstream_desync and backpressure are the incident reasons (7.4) and the only ones the lines judge; the other reasons cross them in normal use. Moving today: client_resync, reconfigure, the bars and indicator series' generation_swap and history_repair, upstream_desync from the alerts topic (6.2.1) and from a delta the hub failed to emit, and backpressure with CV_WS_BACKPRESSURE_ENABLED on. The book feed does not call the hub's upstream_desync trigger yet, and upstream_reconnect, instrument_revision and replay_seek have no caller, so a flat zero for those is not coverage. WsUpstreamDesyncHigh fires above 5 upstream_desync in an hour.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "dashed"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#0072B2",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#E69F00",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "#D55E00",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "id": 11,
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cv-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "round(sum by (reason) (increase(cv_ws_resync_total{env=\"$env\"}[$__range])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "WS resyncs in the range, by reason (lines: 1 and 5 an hour)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
