        "uid": "cv-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Data-frame bytes per second over the open connections: a mean, not the busiest client. Estimated from cv_ws_frame_bytes, kind json or msgpack, sampled 1 in 32 with weight 32, so each subscription's first 31 frames, control frames and system frames are left out and it reads low. Bytes are as encoded for the send, before permessage-deflate and less the span id sp; with the backpressure flag on a frame counts at its encode, so one the ladder drops later is in it. A connection feeds only its own codec, so json and msgpack never count the same frame; the CVWB kinds do, so they are left out. The lines are 23-ws-protocol.md 16.3's server-to-client budget for the reference workspace.",
